{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'npx prisma db update -h'","aggregated_output":"prisma db update → Update your database schema to match your contract\n\n│  Usage\n│    $ prisma db update [options]\n│\n│  Compares the database to the emitted contract and applies the changes that\n│  close the gap, whether or not the database was bootstrapped with `db init`.\n│  Before it applies an operation that would lose data, it asks what the\n│  operation means: --rename keeps the data under a new name, --delete lets it\n│  go. Before it changes who can read or write a model's data, it asks for\n│  --allow. Where nobody can answer, it refuses and lists every question. Use\n│  --dry-run to see the operations and the questions without applying anything.\n│\n│  Options\n│      --db <url>               Database connection string\n│      --dry-run                Preview the planned operations without applying them\n│      --to <contract>          Contract to update to (hash, prefix, ref name, migration dir name, or <dir>^)\n│      --advance-ref <name>     Advance the named ref to the post-command contract hash\n│      --rename <subject>...    Rename a model or field instead of dropping it: old:new, each side Model, namespace.Model, Model.field or namespace.Model.field; repeat for several, applied in order\n│      --delete <subject>...    Let the command lose the data of a model, field or storage name the refusal lists: --delete Model\n│      --allow <subject>...     Let the command change who can read or write a model's data: --allow Model\n│      --convert <subject>...   Not available here: db update has no migration file to fill; use migration plan\n│      --backfill <subject>...  Not available here: db update has no migration file to fill; use migration plan\n│\n│  Global options also apply: --format, --json, --log-level, --verbose,\n│  --quiet, --yes, --confirm, --interactive, --color, --config. Run 'prisma\n│  --help' for details.\n│\n│  Examples\n│    $ prisma db update\n│    $ prisma db update --dry-run\n│    $ prisma db update --delete Legacy\n│    $ prisma db update --rename Profile:User --allow User\n│    $ prisma db update --to production\n│\n│  Docs  https://docs.prisma.io/docs/orm/v8/reference/error-reference/\n\nPrisma agent skills are out of date (installed @prisma/orm-postgres 8.0.0-rc.23, synced none). Run: prisma skills sync\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
