{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"agent_message","text":"**What I Did**\n\n- Added **Prisma ORM** (v5) and **@prisma/client** to the project.  \n- Created `prisma/schema.prisma` defining `User` (unique email, optional name) and `Post` (title, optional content, `published` default false) with a one‑to‑many relation.  \n- Ran `npx prisma db push` – this created the tables in the local PostgreSQL database referenced by `.env` and generated the Prisma client.  \n- Added `script.ts` at the project root that:\n  1. Clears any existing data (so repeated runs are safe).  \n  2. Creates a user with two posts.  \n  3. Prints the created user and then lists every user together with their posts.  \n- Documented the steps in `ANSWER.md` and noted that the script can be run with:\n\n```bash\nnpx tsx script.ts\n```"}}
